---
description: Locate code through the bgts-context-engine MCP server before exploring the repository
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository is indexed in the `{server_name}` MCP server (repository id{repo_plural} {repo_ids}):
a deterministic code graph (symbols, calls, references, imports, types).

- Before searching the tree for a task, call `get_context_for_task` once with the full task text
  and `repo_ids: {repo_ids_json}`. Make it your first action, not something you try after a round of
  grep. `task_text` is the only required argument; the defaults (`max_candidates` 20,
  `max_tokens` 1500) are the tuned ones. You do not need to look up the tool schema first.
- Each item carries `file_id` (`<repo>:<path>`), `line`, `name`, `kind` and a short `content`
  snippet. These are verified locations: open those files directly; do not glob or grep for
  something the result already locates. Search only for what it does not cover - locale files,
  configs and tests are not in the graph.
- The items are places to inspect, not a to-do list. Change only what the task requires; a file
  being listed is not a reason to edit it.
- Never repeat the call with the same text. Call it again only for a distinct sub-problem. If
  `coverage.confidence` is `low`, prefer normal search over another call.
